## Context
Author, 2026-11-01: "I want agentic judgment on which memories likely useful." Skill case notes
(memory/skills/<skill>.md) are pushed at skill load (tickets 1394, 1404, 1405) but nothing maintains
them: in the pilot they are written by hand, and smelt does not write memory/skills/. Smelt already
reads the whole project memory at each consolidation.

## Scope
At each smelt, for each skill that has a case note (and any skill whose memory shows recurring
episodes), re-select the cases by judged usefulness per ticket 1431's principle: dated, sourced, a
"Use:" line each, under the cap. List added and dropped cases with one line of why each in the
smelt report. Smelt proposes; the author's acceptance of the smelt merge request is the review.
No rule writes (AGENTS.md § Project memory boundary).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] skills/smelt describes the case-note curation step
- [ ] One smelt run produces or refreshes at least one case note with its add/drop list
